  "note": "Private test IPA 771, for the maintainer's request of 17 November 2026 (« Lance une ipa avec les derniers pack HD etc.... » after the report on the IPA 765 test: « … toute amélioration doit être mise en œuvre et tous les problèmes trouvés dans les journaux doit être corrigé »). Base: the verified IPA 767 (run 44016455273, IPA dd4ab775); IPA 768 failed (run 44065214671, a resource-only change of neo_texture_catalog taken as a must-change image, fixed in the recipe by 9ac3fabf) and was not recorded. Changes: the S2Arm engine of patches 0001-0077 (verified pin 880d3494: run 44063915936, artifact 14320815741, packagedFingerprint 7bef04e9): 0066 vertex shaders take their base instance from Metal (the vanishing palms of Mario Kart World), 0067-0077 display pacing under the 30 FPS limit, first-use pipelines and translations, storage read-ahead, reuse of textures and snapshots when the game resizes, render-pass splits, encoding, guest waits, the iOS shell and the services; RPCS3 Core 945 replacing Core 943 (verified pin 32cac51c, fingerprint 5914939b; the RPCS3 session's lot of the IPA 767 logs); the catalogue work of 16-17 November promoted from the failed 768 (Cheats & Enhancements 18 sources / 50,600 entries, HD textures 1,319 references, 987 slang presets, the bell's newer-catalogue notification); the S2Arm bridge waits for the end of a game before deleting an earlier preparation. The MeloNX lot after IPA 767 (MeloNX session, at the maintainer's request): MeloNX Core 1df78c52 replacing 58319c2c (verified pin 1021a815, packagedFingerprint fa5ce588: large object heap compaction request under host pressure, the game's own svcBreak journaled) and MoltenVK v1.4.2 with the eight-part recipe patch (pin 38967c0c, binary e3a2504c: a shader module's compressed SPIR-V in an unlinked temporary file). IPA 770 (run 44074184767) failed before compiling: its MeloNX commits were deferred while the recipe already counted their Core gates; not recorded. Build-only delivery: Flutter and native test groups not run (AGENTS.md). Nothing has run on an iPhone; no frame-rate, stutter or rendering claim.",
